/* Creator page configs private (round 48, finding R48-6 in docs/reliability/SECURITY.md). Run only after the deploy that moved public reads to the server (round 48): before it, the creator pages, product pages and OnePages read store_builder_configs and product_page_configs with the anon key, and this part closes that door, so run it earlier and those pages draw their default look until the deploy lands. WHY: the anon key is in every page Storelib serves, and the policy the repository's baseline made (store_builder_configs_public_read and product_page_configs_public_read, and the older "Anyone can view published configs" of scripts/010) let it read every row with a published config through the REST API, draft_config and published_config.headerSettings.contactEmail included; row level security cannot hide a column. Production's policies were made by hand, so this part reads them rather than assuming names. WHAT IT DOES, for each of the two tables that exists: 1. drops every permissive SELECT or ALL policy that is not an owner policy, with a notice naming it, its roles and its USING text; an owner policy is one whose USING reads auth.uid() and creator_id and reads no config column (published_config, draft_config, published_at), so a policy that also lets a published row through is dropped. 2. makes sure the owner can still read and write their own rows: <table>_owner_select, _owner_insert, _owner_update and _owner_delete, for the authenticated role, creator_id in the creators rows whose user_id is (select auth.uid()); each is created only when no policy of that name exists. The editor and the dashboard read with the owner's own session, or with the service role after an ownership check (team members), and the service role passes row level security, so nothing the app does needs more. 3. turns row level security on (a no op where it is on) and takes every privilege on the two tables away from anon, so a policy added later by hand cannot open them to the public key again. Changes no rows. Takes a short lock on each table. Safe to run again: a second run finds nothing to drop and every owner policy there. To check before or after: select policyname, roles, cmd, qual from pg_policies where tablename in ('store_builder_configs','product_page_configs'); */
DO $do$ DECLARE t text; r record; dropped int := 0; BEGIN FOREACH t IN ARRAY ARRAY['store_builder_configs', 'product_page_configs'] LOOP IF to_regclass('public.' || t) IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'part 354: public.% does not exist here, skipped', t; CONTINUE; END IF; FOR r IN SELECT p.policyname, p.roles, p.cmd, p.qual FROM pg_policies p WHERE p.schemaname = 'public' AND p.tablename = t AND p.permissive = 'PERMISSIVE' AND p.cmd IN ('SELECT', 'ALL') AND NOT (coalesce(p.qual, '') ~ 'auth\.uid\(\)' AND coalesce(p.qual, '') ~ 'creator_id' AND coalesce(p.qual, '') !~ '(published_config|draft_config|published_at)') ORDER BY p.policyname LOOP EXECUTE format('DROP POLICY %I ON public.%I', r.policyname, t); dropped := dropped + 1; RAISE NOTICE 'part 354: dropped policy "%" on % (% for %, using %)', r.policyname, t, r.cmd, r.roles, coalesce(r.qual, 'nothing'); END LOOP; END LOOP; RAISE NOTICE 'part 354: % policies that let more than the owner read dropped', dropped; END $do$;
DO $do$ DECLARE t text; BEGIN FOREACH t IN ARRAY ARRAY['store_builder_configs', 'product_page_configs'] LOOP IF to_regclass('public.' || t) IS NULL THEN CONTINUE; END IF; IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_policies WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename = t AND policyname = t || '_owner_select') THEN EXECUTE format('CREATE POLICY %I ON public.%I FOR SELECT TO authenticated USING (creator_id IN (SELECT c.id FROM public.creators c WHERE c.user_id = (SELECT auth.uid())))', t || '_owner_select', t); END IF; IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_policies WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename = t AND policyname = t || '_owner_insert') THEN EXECUTE format('CREATE POLICY %I ON public.%I FOR INSERT TO authenticated WITH CHECK (creator_id IN (SELECT c.id FROM public.creators c WHERE c.user_id = (SELECT auth.uid())))', t || '_owner_insert', t); END IF; IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_policies WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename = t AND policyname = t || '_owner_update') THEN EXECUTE format('CREATE POLICY %I ON public.%I FOR UPDATE TO authenticated USING (creator_id IN (SELECT c.id FROM public.creators c WHERE c.user_id = (SELECT auth.uid()))) WITH CHECK (creator_id IN (SELECT c.id FROM public.creators c WHERE c.user_id = (SELECT auth.uid())))', t || '_owner_update', t); END IF; IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_policies WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename = t AND policyname = t || '_owner_delete') THEN EXECUTE format('CREATE POLICY %I ON public.%I FOR DELETE TO authenticated USING (creator_id IN (SELECT c.id FROM public.creators c WHERE c.user_id = (SELECT auth.uid())))', t || '_owner_delete', t); END IF; EXECUTE format('ALTER TABLE public.%I ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY', t); EXECUTE format('REVOKE ALL ON public.%I FROM anon', t); END LOOP; END $do$;
notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
